From 6c8ebc9ef8336076f8556764b03ce970a18c84b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Caleb=20=E3=83=84=20Everett?= <calebev@amazon.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] river: add hrwm-activation-v1 for window activation requests

xdg-activation-v1 activate requests for windows were dropped, since the
window management protocol has no way to pass them on. Add a small
out-of-tree global, hrwm_activation_v1, that sends activation_requested
for a river_window_v1 to the window manager before the next manage_start.

X11 windows trigger it too: _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW, _NET_WM_STATE_DEMANDS_ATTENTION,
and the ICCCM urgency hint being set.
